<title>GERMANY: Waigel-Germany will meet Maastricht deficit target.</title>
<headline>Waigel-Germany will meet Maastricht deficit target.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel repeated his belief that Germany will meet the Maastricht Treaty deficit target in time to qualify for European monetary union (EMU).</p>
<p>According to the Maastricht Treaty, nations hoping to join monetary union must reduce their budget deficits to at most three percent of gross domestic product.</p>
<p>In 1996 Germany's budget deficit stood at 3.8 percent of GDP.</p>
<p>Speaking about Bonn's efforts to qualify for EMU, Waigel said: &quot;That means we will meet the Maastricht deficit target.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
